@page "/docs/cards"

<Page>
    <DocsExample Title="Cards" ComponentType="typeof(Card)">

        <CodeSnippet SetBackground Component="@typeof(CardsBasic)" Title="Basic Setup">
            <Description>
                As one of the most common elements of UI design, buttons have a very important function of engaging users with your website or system and guiding them in their actions.
            </Description>
        </CodeSnippet>

        <CodeSnippet Component="@typeof(CardsPadding)" Title="Padding">
            <Description>
                    You can change the padding of a newly created card. To do it, use the Size parameter.
                    Cards with the small size are well suited for small items such as snippets, etc., while the large size can be used for large blocks of text. Padding will be automatically reduced on small devices, to fit the screen size.
            </Description>
        </CodeSnippet>

        <CodeSnippet  Component="@typeof(CardsHeader)" Title="Header">
            <Description>
                Use the card header to set a header. Use the card title if you want the header in the body
            </Description>
        </CodeSnippet>

        <CodeSnippet SetBackground Component="@typeof(CardsStatus)" Title="Status">
            <Description>
                Add a status color to your card, either at the top or on the side of the card, to customise it and make it more eye-catching.eader in the body
            </Description>
        </CodeSnippet>
        
        <CodeSnippet SetBackground Component="@typeof(CardsGradient)" Title="Gradient">
            <Description>
                Set Gradient to give the card a gradient background. GradientDirection controls the edge it fades in from and GradientAnimated animates it.
            </Description>
        </CodeSnippet>

        <CodeSnippet SetBackground Component="@typeof(CardsSurface)" Title="Dashed and Transparent">
            <Description>
                Dashed renders a dashed border. Transparent drops the background and shadow, keeping a dashed border.
            </Description>
        </CodeSnippet>

        <CodeSnippet SetBackground Component="@typeof(CardsCustom)" Title="Custom Css Classes">
            <Description>
               Custom css class to card
            </Description>
        </CodeSnippet>

    </DocsExample>
</Page>


